---
layout: layout.njk
title: Winners archive
description: Review recent PAPR winners and the public timestamps that show when each raffle sold out, drew, and published its result.
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <article class="hero-card panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Winners archive</p>
      <h1>Trust builds when results stay easy to find.</h1>
      <p>A completed raffle should not vanish into chat logs. PAPR’s winners area should preserve timing, archive entries, and result summaries so credibility compounds over time.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="hero-aside panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="kicker">Archive rule</p>
      <h2>The result should outlive the hype cycle.</h2>
      <p>Close time, draw time, and publication time should all remain visible on the public archive entry.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel" data-reveal>
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Recent results</p>
        <h2>Archived entries should read like receipts, not marketing blurbs.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="three-up">
      {% for winner in winners %}
      <article class="card winner-card">
        <p class="kicker">{{ winner.winner }}</p>
        <h3>{{ winner.title }}</h3>
        <div class="meta-grid">
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Sellout</small>
            <strong>{{ winner.sellout }}</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Draw</small>
            <strong>{{ winner.draw }}</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Published</small>
            <strong>{{ winner.publish }}</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Proof summary</small>
            <strong>{{ winner.proof }}</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
